<section class="section" aria-labelledby="story">
  <div class="wrap prose">
    <h2 id="story">How the pieces connect</h2>
    <p>I trained as a graphic designer and started as the only designer at LiveText, an education technology platform used by more than 600 colleges and universities. Everything from marketing to product design went through me, and I designed subscription and upgrade flows aimed at moving more people from trial to paid.</p>
    <p>At ConstructConnect I spent nearly ten years in senior product design for a construction data platform with more than 500,000 users. I helped grow the design team from 2 to 12, built and governed the component-based design system, held WCAG 2.1 accessibility standards across engineering squads, and introduced Lean UX and product operating model practices.</p>
    <p>In late 2022 I moved into growth product management, though product and growth work had been part of my role for a while before the title changed. I built the business case for moving from sales-led to product-led growth, took it to VP and C-suite leadership, and then owned the self-serve experience that grew to $10M+ ARR. I also ran a programmatic page system that reached 1.7M pages. From 2024 my primary function sat in Marketing, while I kept shaping product planning and growth strategy.</p>
    <p>That path wasn’t a series of pivots. Each step came from connecting disciplines most companies keep apart: research to design, design to product, product to revenue.</p>
    <p>Since January 2026 I’ve been consulting and contracting on product, design and growth work through <a href="/work-with-me/">RyDev Studio</a>, my consulting practice, while looking for the right full-time role.</p>
  </div>
</section>

