<section class="section" aria-labelledby="beliefs">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head"><h2 id="beliefs">What I believe about the work</h2></div>
    <ul class="principles">
      <li><h3>Outcomes over outputs</h3><p>A feature that doesn’t change behavior or move a business metric isn’t done. Shipping is a checkpoint, not the finish line.</p></li>
      <li><h3>Design is a systems problem</h3><p>A screen isn’t a product. Every component and pattern should make the next decision faster and the next hire’s job easier.</p></li>
      <li><h3>Craft earns trust</h3><p>Precision in the details signals rigor in the decisions. Stakeholders extend strategic trust to people whose work is careful.</p></li>
      <li><h3>Constraints are the brief</h3><p>Budgets, technical limits and organizational friction are the conditions that make a solution real, not obstacles to it.</p></li>
      <li><h3>Discovery is a habit, not a phase</h3><p>Teams that keep talking to customers and testing assumptions make better bets and waste less in development.</p></li>
      <li><h3>Design and product are revenue functions</h3><p>That means owning whether what shipped actually worked, not just whether it shipped.</p></li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

